1087|a|The same; the selfsame; the very same; not different; as, the identical person or thing. ; Uttering sameness or the same truth; expressing in the predicate what is given, or obviously implied, in the subject; tautological.	j:1egy,54,5;1mx9,33,4;1hdy,27,4;14bj,23,4;3fy,18,3;1ovy,11,8;1owa,8,3~1ovy,11,8;1egy,54,5;1mx9,33,4;1hdy,27,4;14bj,23,4;1owa,8,3;3fy,18,3	e:ud5,91,3;29d9,81,6;1m13,77,4;1d3q,75,13;ba,56,5;2cw,53,14;6li,42,4;qha,41,6~2cw,53,14;1d3q,75,13;qha,41,6;29d9,81,6;ba,56,5;6li,42,4;1m13,77,4;ud5,91,3
