108f|v|To make to be the same; to unite or combine in such a manner as to make one; to treat as being one or having the same purpose or effect; to consider as the same in any relation. ; To establish the identity of; to prove to be the same with something described, claimed, or asserted; as, to identify stolen property. ; To become the same; to coalesce in interest, purpose, use, effect, etc.	s:aox,18,2~aox,18,2	d:g7l,42,4;de1,31,3;ncc,30,3~g7l,42,4;de1,31,3;ncc,30,3
